I have two laptops, each running Ubuntu 18.04. One of them will pair 
with Google Home Speakers with no problem.

When the other tries to pair the agent always asks for a pin for me to 
verify on the speaker, which of course I can't, its a speaker. After a 
while it times out with an auth error.

None of the generic pins work, but the point is that on the other laptop 
there is never a request for a pin.

This is standard Ubuntu 18.04 on both. Could it be something about a 
difference in the bluetooth hardware on the laptops?

